Subject: Cantor Declared Field Exact Binding

Description: Bounded correction authority for an explicit attention-language parser that requires exact normalized equality for each unambiguous caller-declared field while preserving literal grounding for undeclared fields and ordinary language.

@ [specification_uuid] fad93ccd-729e-452c-9fe2-18aa63c8f9d2
@ [profile] cantor-declared-field-binding/0.1
@ [source_manifest] C:\Project\Cantor\source_documents\2026-08-18_declared_field_exact_binding\Source_Document_Manifest.sop
@ [predecessor] C:\Project\Cantor\specifications\Cantor_Caller_Stimulus_Argument_Grounding.sop

& [BindingIdentity] distinguishes presence from declared identity
  + literal grounding proves that a selected phrase occurs in caller text
  + exact declared binding proves that a selected value equals one unambiguous structured field supplied by the caller
  + exact binding activates independently for each unambiguous delimited field declared for the selected procedure
  + undeclared arguments retain literal grounding without inferred declarations
  - never: treat either check as truth authorization or external-effect permission

& [DelimitedGrammar] is deliberately small
  + records are separated by semicolon or newline
  + a declaration record begins after whitespace with subject claim before_frame or after_frame
  + the field name is followed by colon or equals and then one nonempty value
  + an unquoted value loses surrounding whitespace and one terminal sentence period
  + a value enclosed by matching single or double quotes loses only those outer quotes
  + internal punctuation and whitespace remain value content before normalization
  + non-declaration records may precede or follow declarations

& [JSONGrammar] is whole-document and closed
  + when trimmed stimulus begins with left brace and ends with right brace it must be unique-key UTF-8 JSON object
  + admitted keys are the selected procedure's required argument names plus optional procedure
  + every required field must be a nonempty string
  + procedure when present must equal selected procedure ID or selected tool name
  + malformed duplicate unknown conflicting or non-string JSON fails closed

& [Activation] is deterministic
  + collect declarations only for the selected procedure's required fields
  + any duplicate selected field fails closed even when the set is incomplete
  + zero declarations returns no exact-binding account and retains literal grounding
  + every unique delimited declaration activates exact binding for that field whether or not other fields are declared
  + whole-document JSON remains closed and requires the complete required field set
  + no field may borrow another field's value

& [Comparison] preserves selected bytes
  + normalize declared and selected values with the existing NFKC casefold whitespace-collapse function
  + require equality for every explicitly declared field
  + mismatch rejects the selected call
  + admitted arguments retain their original schema-valid bytes
  + literal caller-stimulus grounding remains mandatory before exact declared binding

& [Faults] are private and typed
  + needle_declaration_invalid reports malformed ambiguous duplicate unknown or conflicting structured declarations
  + needle_argument_binding_mismatch reports selected values that differ from explicit declarations
  + inner cause contains sorted field names or one bounded structural label and no caller values
  + public wrapping may add existing run identity and Needle confidence
  + all faults occur before Cantor and llama.cpp

& [Compatibility] is measured
  + pinned structured identity and transition fixtures remain exact selections
  + JSON-like key-value line-field and explicit-label corpus cases bind exactly when complete
  + natural questions and incomplete declaration sets retain current literal behavior
  + catalogue procedure hashes threshold and provider behavior remain unchanged

& [Acceptance] is measurable
  + [DFB-001] source and manifest bytes remain exact before implementation
  + [DFB-002] delimited parser accepts colon equals semicolon newline quote and terminal-period forms
  + [DFB-003] JSON parser accepts exact closed objects and optional matching procedure identity
  + [DFB-004] duplicates unknown JSON keys malformed JSON empty values and conflicting procedure identities reject
  + [DFB-005] incomplete delimited declarations bind only present fields and never invent missing fields
  + [DFB-006] every declared field requires normalized equality with its selected argument
  + [DFB-007] mismatch fault discloses field names only and occurs before semantic stages
  + [DFB-008] original argument bytes remain unchanged after successful binding
  + [DFB-009] all local and EVO-X2 runtime tests plus pinned evaluator pass
  + [DFB-010] the observed citation contraction now rejects as needle_argument_binding_mismatch
  + [DFB-011] canonical resolve identity transition and one full route remain successful
  + [DFB-012] refreshed deployment and shared noninterference proof pass

& [SJSProcessingTrace] records seven-fold convergence
  + [fold_1_identity] separates phrase presence from exact declared-field identity
  + [fold_2_language] defines two minimal machine-readable surface grammars
  + [fold_3_honesty] prevents learned contraction from being attributed as the caller's full declaration
  + [fold_4_security] fails closed on complete-set mismatch ambiguity and malformed structured JSON
  + [fold_5_compatibility] preserves literal checks for undeclared fields selected bytes catalogue and threshold
  + [fold_6_data] records declaration activation fields mismatch fault and immutable evidence
  + [fold_7_phase_lock] excludes general parsing synonyms inference effects and schema expansion

& [SJSContradictionResolution] corrects the non-authoritative candidate without rewriting source
  + the preserved observed case declares before_frame and after_frame but does not declare subject with a field label
  + complete-set-only activation would therefore leave the motivating contraction undetected
  + per-declared-field equality is the smallest rule that satisfies the observed case and never infers a missing field
  + complete-set closure remains mandatory for whole-document JSON because JSON presents itself as the entire structured request

